Parked on the f64 hole, NOT on the parse route. The original park ("the
parse.source -> eval route returns validation-error / No flow found in AST")
is FIXED: parse.source now uses the interpreter's own flow_parser, and this
test parses and dispatches. Two things had to change in the test itself — the
invented `file_name` argument is gone, and the source spelled the event
`set_config` while the scope registers `set-config`, so it was event-denied.

What remains, measured 2026-08-07:

    enabled=true ratio=0 count=42

`ratio: 3.5` arrives as 0. bool and i64 are correct. The interpreter reads any
unquoted value containing a `.` as field access `binding.field`
(koru_std/interpreter.kz evaluateExpr), so `3.5` becomes binding `3`, field
`5`; `3` is unbound and the value hands back the string "<unbound:3>", which
the generated dispatcher turns into 0 via `parseFloat(...) catch 0`. The
`catch 0` is what makes it silent rather than loud.

expected.txt asserts the CORRECT value, so this test flips green on its own the
day floats dispatch. It is the only pin on f64 through runtime dispatch.
